 "sources": [
  "GamesRadar: Red Dead Redemption 2 dataminer finds parachuting files they think relate to GTA 6 (Jan 2021; dataminer rollschuh2282, PC version; names skydive@parachute@pack, Chute_Off, Chute_Off_Bag; not found in gta5.exe; Rockstar never confirmed)",
  "Gamepressure: GTA 6 Files in RDR2? This Time It's Parachutes",
  "Charlie INTEL / IBTimes: GTA 6 rumors grow after players find strange files in RDR2 (alternative explanations: leftovers from parallel Rockstar projects, or a GTA 5 port on the newer engine)"
 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Red Dead Redemption 2, a western with parachutes in its files?"
  },
  {
   "text": "A dataminer found parachute references inside the PC version, and GamesRadar reported it."
  },
  {
   "text": "The names include skydive at parachute pack, and chute off bag."
  },
  {
   "text": "Cowboys never skydive, so fans guessed those files belong to GTA 6."
  },
  {
   "text": "GTA 5 already has parachutes, but those names are not in its own files."
  },
  {
   "text": "Other outlets say it's simpler: Rockstar ran several projects, and leftovers slipped in."
  },
  {
   "text": "Rockstar has never confirmed any of it, so treat this as a fan theory."
  },
  {
   "text": "Still, skydiving over Leonida would be wild."
  },
  {
   "text": "So tell us below, do you think Rockstar hid a clue inside"
  }
 ],
